 *
 * <p>Each datagram is read as consecutive cleartext envelopes. Packet numbers are reconstructed per
 * level, then routing, key, range, authentication, duplication and key-epoch precedence is applied.
 * Surviving packets decode their frames through the retained TLS-Attacker frame table; every packet
 * is one transaction that either commits all of its effects or rolls all of them back. Accepted
 * packets are re-encoded as canonical envelopes, hashed and summarized together with the committed
 * snapshot state.
 */
public final class ReceiveAudit {

